.TH TDE\-FIREWALLD 1 "November 2026" "tde-firewalld 0.1.0" "Trinity Desktop Environment"
.SH NAME
tde\-firewalld \- firewalld manager for the Trinity Desktop Environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tde\-firewalld
.RB [ \-\-permanent ]
.RB [ \-\-page
.IR page ]
.RB [ \-\-zone
.IR zone ]
.RI [ "generic TDE and TQt options" ]
.br
.B tdecmshell firewalld
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tde\-firewalld
is a graphical front end for
.BR firewalld (1),
the dynamic firewall daemon. It shows and changes the firewalld
configuration through firewalld's D\-Bus interface on the system bus
.RI ( org.fedoraproject.FirewallD1 ).
.PP
The same user interface is available as a Trinity Control Center module,
found under
.B Security & Privacy \(-> Firewall
or started with
.BR "tdecmshell firewalld" .
.PP
It can:
.IP \(bu 2
show the state and version of firewalld and the active zones;
.IP \(bu 2
change the default zone, panic mode and logging of denied packets;
.IP \(bu 2
allow services and open ports or port ranges in a zone;
.IP \(bu 2
enable masquerading and add port forwarding rules;
.IP \(bu 2
add and remove rich rules;
.IP \(bu 2
bind interfaces and source addresses to zones;
.IP \(bu 2
browse the service definitions known to firewalld;
.IP \(bu 2
edit either the runtime or the permanent configuration, reload the
firewall, and copy the runtime configuration to the permanent one.
.PP
Changes are sent to firewalld immediately. Runtime changes are lost when
firewalld is reloaded or the system is restarted; permanent changes are
saved to
.I /etc/firewalld
and take effect after a reload.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-permanent
Start with the permanent configuration selected instead of the runtime
configuration.
.TP
.BI \-\-page " page"
Page to show at start up: one of
.BR status " (default), " zones ", " services " or " interfaces .
.TP
.BI \-\-zone " zone"
Zone to select on the zones page.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show the list of options, including the generic TDE and TQt options such
as
.B \-\-caption
and
.BR \-\-display .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version information.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
.B tde\-firewalld
runs as an ordinary user and never needs to be started as root.
firewalld checks every request with
.BR polkit (8)
using the actions
.IR org.fedoraproject.FirewallD1.info ,
.IR org.fedoraproject.FirewallD1.config.info ,
.I org.fedoraproject.FirewallD1.config
and
.IR org.fedoraproject.FirewallD1.all .
When authentication is required, the polkit authentication agent of the
session,
.BR polkit\-agent\-tde ,
asks for an administrator password. Starting firewalld from the
application uses the systemd action
.IR org.freedesktop.systemd1.manage\-units .
.PP
If no polkit agent is running, a warning is shown and changes will fail
with "Not authorized".
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/trinity/share/applications/tde/firewalld.desktop
Trinity Control Center module description.
.TP
.I /opt/trinity/lib/trinity/kcm_firewalld.so
The Control Center module.
.TP
.I /etc/firewalld/
Permanent firewalld configuration (written by firewalld, not by this program).
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit\-1/actions/org.fedoraproject.FirewallD1.policy
Default polkit policy of firewalld.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B tde\-firewalld
exits with status 0 when it is closed normally.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open the permanent configuration of the
.I public
zone:
.PP
.RS
.B tde\-firewalld \-\-permanent \-\-page zones \-\-zone public
.RE
.PP
Open the Control Center module on its own:
.PP
.RS
.B tdecmshell firewalld
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tde\-firewalld\-tray (1),
